## 2. Module A: E387 at Re 200k vs NASA TM-4062 (CFD vs public experimental)

SU2 v8.6.0 incompressible RANS, SA (fully turbulent) and SST with Langtry-Menter transition (SST-LM, Tu as measured in the LTPT), own C-mesh with first-cell y+ max {{e387.yplus_max:.2f}} over {{e387.n_runs_reported}} reported runs, three systematically refined grids at alpha 4. A run counts in error statistics only when it meets the residual or Cauchy criterion; {{e387.n_runs_unsteady}} runs ended unsteady at the iteration cap and are reported with their oscillation half-amplitude.

{{file:results/cfd/VALIDATION.md#Validation}}

**Laminar separation bubble (SST-LM vs TM-4062 oil flow, chord fractions).**

{{file:results/cfd/VALIDATION.md#Bubble}}

**Grid convergence (Celik et al. 2008).**

{{file:results/cfd/VALIDATION.md#GCI}}

**Reading.** The fully turbulent SA model over-predicts drag at every alpha because it has no laminar run and no bubble; this is the pre-registered physics story (V07). SST-LM reproduces the alpha 4 bubble location within {{e387.lm.re200k.a4.xs_err_c:+.3f}}c (separation) and {{e387.lm.re200k.a4.xr_err_c:+.3f}}c (reattachment) and the time-mean Cd within {{e387.lm.re200k.a4.cd_err_pct:+.1f}}%, but on the coarse and medium grids it never reached a steady state, so by the pre-registered rule those runs are outside error statistics and V05, V06 and V08 fail. A URANS treatment of the bubble is deferred (GAPS.md).

