## 4. Module C: multi-fidelity drag correction (low-order vs public experimental)

A correction to XFOIL (Ncrit 9) drag, log(Cd_exp / Cd_xfoil) regressed on XFOIL outputs and section geometry, chosen by inner GroupKFold and scored leave-one-family-out over {{mf.n_families}} UIUC airfoil families ({{mf.n_points}} identical airfoil, Re, Cl points). E387 and SD7037 families never enter training.

| Tool | Cd MAPE |
|---|---|
| corrected XFOIL | {{mf.cd_mape_corrected_pct:.2f}}% |
| raw XFOIL Ncrit 9 | {{mf.cd_mape_xfoil_pct:.2f}}% |
| NeuralFoil 0.3.3 xxlarge | {{mf.cd_mape_neuralfoil_pct:.2f}}% |
| held-out test airfoils: corrected / raw XFOIL | {{mf.test.cd_mape_corrected_pct:.2f}}% / {{mf.test.cd_mape_xfoil_pct:.2f}}% |
| E387 Re 100k signed Cd error: raw XFOIL / corrected | {{mf.e387.re100k.cd_err_xfoil_pct:+.1f}}% / {{mf.e387.re100k.cd_err_corrected_pct:+.1f}}% |

The reduction against raw XFOIL is {{mf.cd_mape_reduction_pct:.1f}}%; the pre-registered bar asks for a ratio of at most 0.75, so V11 fails by a small margin while the corrected model beats NeuralFoil on the same points. StratoGlide's XFOIL validation failed its own 15% bar at Re 100k on E387 with Ncrit 5 (its pre-registered rule); FlightLoop runs Ncrit 9 and 11 at matched UIUC points, so the two numbers are not the same metric.

