## 6. Module E: system identification

**Synthetic (labelled synthetic).** {{sysid.synth.n_seeds}} seeds of the StratoGlide design model in FlightLoop's 6-DOF with MIL-F-8785C light turbulence and sensor noise; glide force method for CD0 and k, equation error for the longitudinal derivatives, output error reported alongside.

| Parameter | Median abs. error, equation error / force method | Median abs. error, output error |
|---|---|---|
| CD0 | {{sysid.synth.cd0_median_err_pct:.2f}}% | n/a (glide method only) |
| k | {{sysid.synth.k_median_err_pct:.2f}}% | n/a (glide method only) |
| CLa | {{sysid.synth.cla_median_err_pct:.2f}}% | {{sysid.synth.oe_cla_median_err_pct:.2f}}% |
| Cma | {{sysid.synth.cma_median_err_pct:.2f}}% | {{sysid.synth.oe_cma_median_err_pct:.2f}}% |
| Cmde | {{sysid.synth.cmde_median_err_pct:.2f}}% | {{sysid.synth.oe_cmde_median_err_pct:.2f}}% |
| Cmq | {{sysid.synth.cmq_median_err_pct:.2f}}% | {{sysid.synth.oe_cmq_median_err_pct:.2f}}% |

95% CI coverage over seeds: CD0 {{sysid.synth.coverage_cd0_pct:.0f}}%, CLa {{sysid.synth.coverage_cla_pct:.0f}}%, Cma {{sysid.synth.coverage_cma_pct:.0f}}% (V16 fails; the per-flight pitot scale error is not in the regression standard errors). Findings: the energy-method CD0 is biased by vertical gusts ({{sysid.synth.cd0_energy_median_err_pct:.1f}}% with gusts, {{sysid.synth.cd0_energy_calm_median_err_pct:.1f}}% calm); alpha estimated without a vane biases CLa by {{sysid.synth.novane_bias_cla_pct:+.0f}}%; at 18 km the glide CD0 median error is {{sysid.synth.alt18km_cd0_median_err_pct:.2f}}%.

**CMU ALFA (public experimental).** Energy-method glide polar on post-engine-failure windows of {{sysid.alfa.n_flights_used}} flights ({{sysid.alfa.n_segments_used}} windows), bootstrap over flights.

| Quantity | Flight | 95% CI | AVL (approximate geometry) |
|---|---|---|---|
| CD0 (airframe + stopped prop) | {{sysid.alfa.cd0:.4f}} | {{sysid.alfa.cd0_ci_lo:.4f}} to {{sysid.alfa.cd0_ci_hi:.4f}} | n/a (inviscid) |
| k | {{sysid.alfa.k:.3f}} | {{sysid.alfa.k_ci_lo:.3f}} to {{sysid.alfa.k_ci_hi:.3f}} | {{sysid.alfa.k_avl:.4f}} |
| span efficiency e | {{sysid.alfa.e_flight:.3f}} | from k | {{sysid.alfa.e_avl:.4f}} |

The flight k includes every lift-dependent drag term (profile drag growth, trim, prop wake), not only induced drag, and mass and wing area are retailer figures; the CD0 interval spans zero. Parsers: {{logs.px4_ok}} public PX4 ULog and {{logs.ardupilot_ok}} ArduPilot .bin files reach the full canonical schema.

## 7. Module F: next-iteration engine and correlation report (synthetic)

`stubs/inject.py` draws a discrepancy (CD0 growth, aft CG, elevator effectiveness), applies it to the design model and seals it; the engine sees only the flight-1 logs and the design model (its file access is audited), identifies, applies first-order design rules and predicts flight 2.

| Metric over {{loop.blind.n_seeds}} blind seeds | Value |
|---|---|
| CD0 delta error, max | {{loop.blind.max_cd0_delta_err_pp:.2f}} pp |
| static margin delta error, max | {{loop.blind.max_sm_delta_err_mac_pct:.2f}}% MAC |
| next-flight sink error reduction, median | {{loop.blind.sink_err_reduction_pct:.1f}}% |
| next-flight trim error reduction, median | {{loop.blind.trim_err_reduction_pct:.1f}}% |
| secondary (post hoc): air-relative sink, all glides / inside envelope | {{loop.blind.secondary.air_all_reduction_pct:.1f}}% / {{loop.blind.secondary.air_env_reduction_pct:.1f}}% |
| secondary (post hoc): trim inside envelope | {{loop.blind.secondary.trim_env_reduction_pct:.1f}}% |

The recovery parts of V18 pass; the next-flight prediction part fails on the pre-registered metric (HONEST_LOG 14 and the V18 entry give the cause: inertial sink carries the air-mass vertical velocity, and the two slowest glides fly beyond the linear envelope).

